  "description": "<h2>About the Project</h2>\n<p>The Citizen-Centred Artificial Intelligence CDT places people and communities at the centre of AI research. Its doctoral training route is designed around the development and use of AI systems, with funding terms that differ between home and international applicants.</p>\n<h2>Research Areas</h2>\n<ul><li>Artificial intelligence</li><li>Human-centred technology</li><li>Computer science</li></ul>\n<h2>Funding and duration</h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1.45\"><thead style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Component</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Award or position</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">PhD scholarship / studentship</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Stipend / salary</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Home: GBP 30,000/year (2027/28); international: UKRI rate</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Duration</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Four years</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Eligibility and Requirements</h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1.45\"><thead style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Criterion</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Requirement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Applicant eligibility</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Programme and project criteria apply; see official eligibility guidance</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Further conditions</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Northumbria-led four-year programme; enhanced home and standard international stipend differ.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Application dates</h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1.45\"><thead style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Component</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Recruitment status</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Upcoming: opens 12 October 2026</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Deadline / consideration round</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">11 January 2027</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Location</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">United Kingdom</td></tr><tr></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>About Northumbria University</h2>\n<p>Northumbria is a UK university with postgraduate research across its academic schools. It leads the Citizen-Centred Artificial Intelligence doctoral training programme, bringing research in AI together with questions about its use in society.</p>\n<p><strong>Official details:</strong> <a href=\"https://ccai-cdt.ac.uk/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Read the programme or project information</a></p>\n<p><strong>Application route:</strong> <a href=\"https://ccai-cdt.ac.uk/apply/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Follow the official application instructions</a></p>\n<p><strong>2026/27 UKRI reference rate:</strong> the minimum UKRI doctoral stipend is £21,805 per year, tax-free (London institutions +£2,000), effective 1 October 2026.</p><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Submit your application through the official portal before the deadline: 11 January 2027. Read the eligibility requirements carefully and prepare all requested documents — early applications are strongly recommended for competitive awards.</p><p><a href=\"https://ccai-cdt.ac.uk/apply/\">Open the official application page ↗</a></p><h2>Application guides</h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://nextapply.co.uk/articles/how-to-read-phd-job-advertisement-before-applying\">How to Read a PhD Job Advert: Funding, Eligibility and Application Steps</a></li><li><a href=\"https://nextapply.co.uk/articles/how-to-write-academic-cv-phd-applications-sample\">Academic CV for PhD Applications: Structure and an Example</a></li><li><a href=\"https://nextapply.co.uk/articles/how-to-apply-uk-student-visa-step-by-step-2026-2027\">UK Student Visa Application: CAS, Documents and Financial Evidence</a></li></ul>",
